  "result": "I fixed it. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:31` was comparing each line's **name** to the sku you passed in, not its sku. Calling `remove('sku-1')` looked for an item named `'sku-1'`, but the item is named `'Widget'`, so nothing was removed.\n\nThe fix is one line:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\nThis matches `Cart.add`, which already looks lines up by `item.sku`.\n\n**Results:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- All 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nNone of the existing tests calls `Cart.remove`, which is how this got through. I can add a regression test if you'd like.",
